IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sda-common`
IMPORT `taa-procedure`

-- Taxation Administration Act 1996 (SA) -- cases for the interest, penalty tax, objection and appeal core
-- (taa-procedure.l4).
--
-- Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text (as at 2019-10-03; a later version exists), with the
-- interest and penalty arithmetic also done in an independent calculator written from ss 25-27 and 30-32 (scratchpad
-- au-sa-1/hand.py), never copied from this encoding's output. Dates were counted on a calendar. Regulative rules are
-- asserted with EVALTRACE where the trace ends FULFILLED, and #TRACEd with an "-- expect:" line where it ends in a
-- breach or a pending obligation. Clock: days. The market rate is an INPUT (4.35% and 4.1% are example figures, not the
-- gazetted ones). The s 33 cases were added in the fix of 24 October 2026.
--
-- Based on content from the South Australian Legislation website (CC BY 4.0). Not the official text. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases -- the taxpayer and objector`

§§ `ss 25-27 -- interest`

#ASSERT `the interest rate under Part 5, per cent a year` 4.35 EQUALS 12.35
-- $26 830 unpaid for 365 days at 4.35% + 8%: $3 313.505.
#ASSERT `the interest on a tax default` 26830 365 4.35 EQUALS 3313.505
-- $29 580 for 200 days at 4.1% + 8%: 715 836/365, about $1 961.19.
#ASSERT `the interest on a tax default` 29580 200 4.1 EQUALS 715836 DIVIDED BY 365
-- s 27: $1 000 for 30 days at 12% is $9.86, under $20, so nil.
#ASSERT `the interest on a tax default` 1000 30 4 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the interest on a tax default` 26830 0 4.35 EQUALS 0

§§ `ss 30-32 -- penalty tax`

#ASSERT `the most penalty tax on a tax default` 29580 `a tax default that is not deliberate` FALSE `no disclosure and no obstruction` EQUALS 7395
#ASSERT `the most penalty tax on a tax default` 29580 `a deliberate tax default` FALSE `no disclosure and no obstruction` EQUALS 22185
#ASSERT `the most penalty tax on a tax default` 29580 `a tax default that is not deliberate` FALSE `a sufficient disclosure while not subject to a tax audit` EQUALS 1479
#ASSERT `the most penalty tax on a tax default` 29580 `a tax default that is not deliberate` FALSE `a sufficient disclosure while subject to a tax audit` EQUALS 5916
#ASSERT `the most penalty tax on a tax default` 29580 `a deliberate tax default` FALSE `obstructive conduct while subject to a tax audit` EQUALS 26622
-- s 30(2): not deliberate and reasonable care taken: nil.
#ASSERT `the most penalty tax on a tax default` 29580 `a tax default that is not deliberate` TRUE `no disclosure and no obstruction` EQUALS 0
-- s 32: 25% of $60 is $15, under $20, so nil; so is 5% of $300.
#ASSERT `the most penalty tax on a tax default` 60 `a tax default that is not deliberate` FALSE `no disclosure and no obstruction` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the most penalty tax on a tax default` 300 `a tax default that is not deliberate` FALSE `a sufficient disclosure while not subject to a tax audit` EQUALS 0

§§ `s 33 -- time for payment of penalty tax`

-- Clock: days from service of the assessment. Penalty tax assessed with 30 days to pay: paid on day 20, or on day 30
-- (the last day of the period), fulfilled. None assessed: no obligation.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 33 -- pay the penalty tax within the period specified in the assessment` TRUE 30) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the taxpayer` `pay the penalty tax` 20)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 33 -- pay the penalty tax within the period specified in the assessment` TRUE 30) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the taxpayer` `pay the penalty tax` 30)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 33 -- pay the penalty tax within the period specified in the assessment` FALSE 30) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL 40)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the taxpayer, "TAA s 33: penalty tax must be paid within the period specified in the assessment; ..." (unpaid on day 31)
#TRACE `s 33 -- pay the penalty tax within the period specified in the assessment` TRUE 30 AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 31)

§§ `ss 82, 86, 87 -- objections`

#ASSERT `an objection may be lodged against` `an assessment of duty`
#ASSERT `an objection may be lodged against` `a decision concerning a refund of duty`
#ASSERT `an objection may be lodged against` `another reviewable decision of the Commissioner`
#ASSERT NOT (`an objection may be lodged against` `a compromise assessment`)
#ASSERT NOT (`an objection may be lodged against` `a decision declared non-reviewable`)
-- Served on 1 March 2026: 60 days after is 30 April 2026; a late objection may be permitted up to 1 March 2027.
#ASSERT `the last day to object (s 86)` (YMD 2026 3 1) EQUALS YMD 2026 4 30
#ASSERT `the last day a late objection may be permitted (s 87)` (YMD 2026 3 1) EQUALS YMD 2027 3 1
#ASSERT `the objection is lodged in time` (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 4 30) FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`the objection is lodged in time` (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 5 1) FALSE)
#ASSERT `the objection is lodged in time` (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 5 1) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the objection is lodged in time` (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2027 3 2) TRUE)

§§ `ss 92-95 -- appeals`

-- s 93: half the assessed tax of $29 580 is $14 790.
#ASSERT `the tax to be paid before appealing (s 93)` 29580 EQUALS 14790
#ASSERT `the s 93 payment condition is met` 29580 14790 FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`the s 93 payment condition is met` 29580 14000 FALSE)
#ASSERT `the s 93 payment condition is met` 29580 0 TRUE
-- Determination served on 10 June 2026: appeal by 9 August 2026; a late appeal may be allowed up to 10 June 2027.
#ASSERT `the last day to appeal (s 94)` (YMD 2026 6 10) EQUALS YMD 2026 8 9
#ASSERT `the last day the Supreme Court may allow a late appeal (s 95)` (YMD 2026 6 10) EQUALS YMD 2027 6 10
-- s 94(2): 95 days undetermined and 14 days' notice given: yes; 10 days' notice, or 80 days, or determined: no.
#ASSERT `an appeal may be made now on an undetermined objection (s 94(2))` 95 FALSE 14
#ASSERT NOT (`an appeal may be made now on an undetermined objection (s 94(2))` 95 FALSE 10)
#ASSERT NOT (`an appeal may be made now on an undetermined objection (s 94(2))` 80 FALSE 14)
#ASSERT NOT (`an appeal may be made now on an undetermined objection (s 94(2))` 95 TRUE 14)

§§ `Part 10 -- object, then appeal (regulative)`

-- Objection on day 30, determination served on day 90, appeal on day 140 (within 60 days of day 90).
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`Part 10 -- object within 60 days, then appeal within 60 days of the determination` `an assessment of duty` 60) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the objector` `lodge a written notice of objection with the Minister` 30), (EVENT `the Minister` `give written notice of the determination of the objection` 90), (EVENT `the objector` `appeal to the Supreme Court` 140)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- No appeal after the determination: not a breach.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`Part 10 -- object within 60 days, then appeal within 60 days of the determination` `an assessment of duty` 60) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the objector` `lodge a written notice of objection with the Minister` 30), (EVENT `the Minister` `give written notice of the determination of the objection` 90), (WAITUNTIL 200)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- An objection on day 70, out of time: the Minister owes nothing.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`Part 10 -- object within 60 days, then appeal within 60 days of the determination` `an assessment of duty` 60) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the objector` `lodge a written notice of objection with the Minister` 70)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- With the Minister's permission (s 87), say 200 days allowed, the same objection is in time.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`Part 10 -- object within 60 days, then appeal within 60 days of the determination` `an assessment of duty` 200) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the objector` `lodge a written notice of objection with the Minister` 70), (EVENT `the Minister` `give written notice of the determination of the objection` 120), (WAITUNTIL 181)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- A compromise assessment cannot be objected to.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`Part 10 -- object within 60 days, then appeal within 60 days of the determination` `a compromise assessment` 60) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL 10)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: the Minister's written notice of the determination, pending (objection in time on day 30)
#TRACE `Part 10 -- object within 60 days, then appeal within 60 days of the determination` `an assessment of duty` 60 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the objector` DOES `lodge a written notice of objection with the Minister` AT 30
-- expect: the objector's appeal still open (determination served on day 90, now day 120)
#TRACE `Part 10 -- object within 60 days, then appeal within 60 days of the determination` `an assessment of duty` 60 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the objector` DOES `lodge a written notice of objection with the Minister` AT 30
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `give written notice of the determination of the objection` AT 90
    (WAITUNTIL 120)
